  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale:**  \n   We evaluate existing records and identify that the current solution uses SLSQP optimization with stochastic restarts. To improve, we employ a hybrid algorithm combining Differential Evolution (DE) for global optimization with Nelder-Mead for local refinement. This leverages DE's ability to explore global optima while ensuring precise local minima. The primary bottleneck addressed is local optima trapping, which DE helps circumvent through population-based exploration.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification:**  \n   - **Objective:** Minimize \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k))  dx \\), approximated by \\( \\max(\\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, \\text{mode}=\"full\") \\times (2.0/n) \\).\n   - **Constraints:**  \n     - \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\) for all \\( i \\),  \n     - \\( \\sum h_i = 1 \\times \\text{n\\_points}/2 \\) (ensured via projection).  \n   - **Formulation:**  \n     Represent \\( h \\) as an \\( n \\)-length vector. Use \\( \\text{DE} \\) to minimize \\( C_5 \\), employing analytical gradients where available and projected gradients otherwise. The initial grid (80 points) is used to seed resolutions, and crossover mutations transfer structure between scales.\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure:**  \n   - **Input:** `seed, budget_s`  \n   - **Steps:**  \n     1. **Grid Generation:** Start with 80-point parent, upscale via interpolation.  \n     2. **DE Setup:**  \n        - Define objective: \\( \\text{C5}(h) = \\max(\\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h)) \\times (2.0/n) \\), projected to feasible set.  \n        - Bounds: \\([0, 1]\\) for all \\( h_i \\).  \n        - DE Parameters: Mutation factor \\( F = 0.8 \\), crossover rate \\( CR = 0.7 \\).  \n     3. **DE Execution:**  \n        - Run DE with \\( 20 \\) individuals (population size).  \n        - Monitor time: Break if \\( \\text{time} > \\text{budget\\_s} \\).  \n     4. **Local Refinement:** Use Nelder-Mead with Hessian approximation on DE's output.  \n     5. **Fallback Logic:** Keep best candidate even after refactoring.  \n     6. **Termination:** Return best \\( C_5 \\) and \\( h \\).  \n\n4. **Search Choices:**  \n   - **Initial Points:** \\( 20 \\) for DE.  \n   - **Mutation Strategy:** Best/1 EXP perturbation.  \n   - **Adaptive Budget:** \\( \\text{budget\\_per\\_grid} = \\text{budget\\_s} / \\sqrt{\\text{n\\_grid}} \\) (adjust based on n).  \n   - **Grid Sizes:** \\( 80, 96, 112, 128, \\ldots \\) (multiples of 8).  \n\n5. **Compute Budget & Robustness:**  \n   - **Time Estimation:** \\( O(\\text{popsize} \\times n^2 \\log n) \\) due to FFT correlation.  \n   - **Fallback:** Preserve parent distribution if no progress.  \n   - **Validaton:** Clip solutions and reproject after DE to ensure safety.  \n\n6. **Validation & Output:**  \n   - **Feasibility Check:** \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\) and \\( \\sum h_i = n/2 \\).  \n   - **Objective Matching:** Use exact same `_c5_from_h` function for comparison.  \n   - **Code Structure:** Use separate DE and refinement functions without global dependencies (lambdas are disallowed).",
